Another potential issue regarding the static function: `String(row[0])` and `String(result.get(...))` inside _fail/_code — String() casts are a special form, so they're fine.

`PackedStringArray()` inside a static in ConfigGate — it's a constructor special form, so no problem.

`RegEx.new()` inside a static — no problem (it's class instantiation).

`entry["id"]` inside `var sid: String = element["id"]` — the Variant→String implicit conversion on typed var assignment needs a valid conversion, and at runtime the JSON returns a String, so it's OK.

Also `id_regex.search(value)` returns a RegExMatch — typed as `var match_result: RegExMatch = id_regex.search(value)`; the search returns a Variant (RegExMatch or null) — typed assignment from null to an object type is permitted.

